{"subjectId":"data-science","id":"text-encoding","title":"Encoding Text as Numbers","group":"Natural Language Processing","order":21,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Models work with numbers, not words. The simplest encoding gives every word in the vocabulary an ID — then each sentence becomes a list of IDs, and can be turned back.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-numbers\"></i>Build a vocabulary</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>corpus = (\"India, officially the Republic of India, is a country in South Asia. \"\n          \"It is the seventh-largest country by area, the second-most populous country, \"\n          \"and the most populous democracy in the world. \"\n          \"In the Indian Ocean, India is in the vicinity of Sri Lanka and the Maldives.\")\n\nfrom nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize, sent_tokenize\nfrom nltk.corpus import stopwords\n\nstop = set(stopwords.words(\"english\"))\ndef keep(word):\n    return word.lower() not in stop and len(word) &gt;= 2      # drop stop words and punctuation\n\nwords = [w.lower() for w in word_tokenize(corpus) if keep(w)]\nvocab = sorted(set(words))                                   # sorted → same IDs every run\nword_to_num = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(vocab, start=1)}\nnum_to_word = {i: w for w, i in word_to_num.items()}\nprint(len(vocab), vocab[:4])                                 # 18 ['area', 'asia', 'country', 'democracy']</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Correction</div><p>The notebook builds the vocabulary from <code>list(set(words))</code> — sets have no fixed order, so the IDs change every run. Sort first to make the mapping reproducible.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-exchange\"></i>Encode and decode</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>corpus = (\"India, officially the Republic of India, is a country in South Asia. \"\n          \"It is the seventh-largest country by area, the second-most populous country, \"\n          \"and the most populous democracy in the world. \"\n          \"In the Indian Ocean, India is in the vicinity of Sri Lanka and the Maldives.\")\n\nfrom nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize, sent_tokenize\nfrom nltk.corpus import stopwords\n\nstop = set(stopwords.words(\"english\"))\nkeep = lambda w: w.lower() not in stop and len(w) &gt;= 2\nvocab = sorted({w.lower() for w in word_tokenize(corpus) if keep(w)})\nword_to_num = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(vocab, start=1)}\nnum_to_word = {i: w for w, i in word_to_num.items()}\n\nencoded = [[word_to_num[w.lower()] for w in word_tokenize(s) if keep(w)] for s in sent_tokenize(corpus)]\nprint(encoded[0])                                            # [5, 10, 12, 5, 3, 15, 2]\nprint(\" \".join(num_to_word[n] for n in encoded[0]))          # india officially republic india country south asia</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list\"></i>Keeping every word</h3>\n<p>To decode back to the full sentence, keep stop words and drop only punctuation. The vocabulary grows, but nothing is lost except capitalisation and punctuation:</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>corpus = (\"India, officially the Republic of India, is a country in South Asia. \"\n          \"It is the seventh-largest country by area, the second-most populous country, \"\n          \"and the most populous democracy in the world. \"\n          \"In the Indian Ocean, India is in the vicinity of Sri Lanka and the Maldives.\")\n\nfrom nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize, sent_tokenize\nis_word = lambda w: any(c.isalpha() for c in w)\nvocab = sorted({w.lower() for w in word_tokenize(corpus) if is_word(w)})\nword_to_num = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(vocab, start=1)}\nnum_to_word = {i: w for w, i in word_to_num.items()}\nfirst = sent_tokenize(corpus)[0]\nids = [word_to_num[w.lower()] for w in word_tokenize(first) if is_word(w)]\nprint(\" \".join(num_to_word[i] for i in ids))   # india officially the republic of india is a country in south asia</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-chart-bar\"></i>Bag of words / counts</h3><p><code>CountVectorizer</code> — how often each vocabulary word occurs (see <em>Naive Bayes</em>).</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-scale\"></i>TF-IDF</h3><p>Counts weighted down for words common across all documents.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-brain\"></i>Word embeddings</h3><p>Dense vectors where similar words are close (Word2Vec, GloVe) — what neural networks and LLMs build on.</p></div></div></section>"}